1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,440
June 2018

2
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,400
Twelve boys from a youth football team go

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,480
exploring a cave in northern Thailand,

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,971
with their young coach

5
00:00:18,121 --> 00:00:19,071
While they are inside,

6
00:00:19,071 --> 00:00:21,022
heavy rain begins to fall

7
00:00:21,172 --> 00:00:23,772
The water rises fast and blocks the way out

8
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:24,600
Outside,

9
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,360
their families wait at the cave entrance,

10
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,220
praying

11
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:27,840
For days,

12
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,920
nobody knows if they are still alive,

13
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:32,047
deep inside a flooded mountain

14
00:00:32,197 --> 00:00:33,627
What followed was one of the most daring

15
00:00:33,627 --> 00:00:35,387
rescues ever attempted

16
00:00:35,638 --> 00:00:37,548
This is the true story of the Thai cave

17
00:00:37,548 --> 00:00:38,668
rescue

18
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,500
The boys were between eleven and sixteen years

19
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:44,860
old,

20
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:47,460
members of a team called the Wild Boars

21
00:00:47,909 --> 00:00:48,979
They lived in Mae Sai,

22
00:00:48,979 --> 00:00:50,739
a small town in northern Thailand,

23
00:00:50,739 --> 00:00:52,914
close to the border with Myanmar

24
00:00:53,064 --> 00:00:54,374
After football practice,

25
00:00:54,374 --> 00:00:56,614
they rode their bikes to the Tham Luang cave

26
00:00:56,614 --> 00:00:58,374
with their twenty-five-year-old assistant

27
00:00:58,374 --> 00:00:59,430
coach

28
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,050
It was a trip they had made before,

29
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:02,925
as a fun adventure

30
00:01:03,075 --> 00:01:04,945
It was one of the longest caves in Thailand,

31
00:01:04,945 --> 00:01:06,865
with tunnels stretching for miles under a

32
00:01:06,865 --> 00:01:07,985
mountain

33
00:01:08,149 --> 00:01:10,259
The cave is about ten kilometers long,

34
00:01:10,259 --> 00:01:11,779
full of narrow passages,

35
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:13,539
chambers and tunnels

36
00:01:14,013 --> 00:01:15,723
They planned to stay for about an hour,

37
00:01:15,723 --> 00:01:17,822
and brought almost no food

38
00:01:17,972 --> 00:01:19,962
A sign at the entrance warned visitors not to

39
00:01:19,962 --> 00:01:21,402
go in during the rainy season,

40
00:01:21,402 --> 00:01:23,314
from July to November

41
00:01:23,464 --> 00:01:26,064
But the rainy season was about to begin

42
00:01:26,494 --> 00:01:28,364
Nobody knew that this short trip would last

43
00:01:28,364 --> 00:01:29,804
eighteen days

44
00:01:33,550 --> 00:01:35,020
While they explored deep inside,

45
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:37,620
heavy monsoon rain began to fall

46
00:01:37,846 --> 00:01:39,716
Rainwater soaked through the mountain above,

47
00:01:39,716 --> 00:01:42,143
and poured in from many directions

48
00:01:42,293 --> 00:01:44,003
Water poured into the cave and flooded the

49
00:01:44,003 --> 00:01:45,882
narrow tunnels behind them

50
00:01:46,032 --> 00:01:48,062
Parts of the tunnel filled with water all the

51
00:01:48,062 --> 00:01:49,621
way to the ceiling

52
00:01:49,771 --> 00:01:51,081
They moved deeper and deeper,

53
00:01:51,081 --> 00:01:52,896
looking for higher ground

54
00:01:53,046 --> 00:01:55,613
They had only a few flashlights with them

55
00:01:55,763 --> 00:01:56,233
Finally,

56
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:58,073
they climbed onto a muddy slope,

57
00:01:58,073 --> 00:02:00,673
about four kilometers from the entrance

58
00:02:01,035 --> 00:02:02,585
There was little space and little air,

59
00:02:02,585 --> 00:02:04,545
but at least the water could not reach them

60
00:02:04,545 --> 00:02:05,471
there

61
00:02:05,621 --> 00:02:06,171
Outside,

62
00:02:06,171 --> 00:02:07,971
their bikes were found at the cave entrance

63
00:02:07,971 --> 00:02:09,975
The search had begun

64
00:02:10,125 --> 00:02:11,275
Parents rushed to the cave,

65
00:02:11,275 --> 00:02:12,395
and stayed there,

66
00:02:12,395 --> 00:02:14,155
day and night

67
00:02:17,583 --> 00:02:18,013
Inside,

68
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:19,293
it was completely dark,

69
00:02:19,293 --> 00:02:20,673
and cold

70
00:02:20,823 --> 00:02:22,533
They huddled together on the muddy slope,

71
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:24,133
to stay warm

72
00:02:24,283 --> 00:02:25,153
They had no food,

73
00:02:25,153 --> 00:02:27,233
so they drank clean water dripping from the

74
00:02:27,233 --> 00:02:28,627
cave walls

75
00:02:28,777 --> 00:02:29,607
To save the batteries,

76
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:31,327
they used their flashlights as little as

77
00:02:31,327 --> 00:02:32,447
possible

78
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:34,480
Their coach had once trained as a monk,

79
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,000
and taught the boys to meditate,

80
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,392
to stay calm and save energy

81
00:02:38,542 --> 00:02:40,252
Breathing slowly and sitting still,

82
00:02:40,252 --> 00:02:41,612
they used less energy,

83
00:02:41,612 --> 00:02:43,048
and less air

84
00:02:43,198 --> 00:02:44,668
They took turns digging at the walls,

85
00:02:44,668 --> 00:02:46,961
hoping to find another way out

86
00:02:47,111 --> 00:02:47,981
They dug a few meters,

87
00:02:47,981 --> 00:02:49,922
but the rock was too hard

88
00:02:50,072 --> 00:02:50,702
Days passed,

89
00:02:50,702 --> 00:02:52,859
with no sign of rescue

90
00:02:53,009 --> 00:02:53,999
Inside the mountain,

91
00:02:53,999 --> 00:02:56,239
they had no idea that thousands of people were

92
00:02:56,239 --> 00:02:58,319
already looking for them

93
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:02,060
Outside,

94
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,020
Thai Navy divers tried to swim in,

95
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,186
but the current was too strong

96
00:03:06,336 --> 00:03:08,046
The Thai Navy set up a base inside the

97
00:03:08,046 --> 00:03:08,366
cave,

98
00:03:08,366 --> 00:03:09,406
and kept trying,

99
00:03:09,406 --> 00:03:10,959
day after day

100
00:03:11,109 --> 00:03:11,539
Soon,

101
00:03:11,539 --> 00:03:13,939
experts arrived from all over the world:

102
00:03:13,939 --> 00:03:14,859
cave divers,

103
00:03:14,859 --> 00:03:15,499
soldiers,

104
00:03:15,499 --> 00:03:17,259
engineers and doctors

105
00:03:17,762 --> 00:03:18,912
Teams came from Britain,

106
00:03:18,912 --> 00:03:20,032
the United States,

107
00:03:20,032 --> 00:03:20,912
Australia,

108
00:03:20,912 --> 00:03:21,552
China,

109
00:03:21,552 --> 00:03:23,952
Japan and many other countries

110
00:03:24,136 --> 00:03:26,326
Huge pumps worked day and night to pull water

111
00:03:26,326 --> 00:03:27,655
out of the cave

112
00:03:27,805 --> 00:03:30,155
Water from the pumps was sent into nearby rice

113
00:03:30,155 --> 00:03:30,675
fields,

114
00:03:30,675 --> 00:03:32,435
flooding farmers' crops

115
00:03:32,949 --> 00:03:34,859
Volunteers searched the jungle on the mountain

116
00:03:34,859 --> 00:03:36,852
above for another way in

117
00:03:37,002 --> 00:03:38,672
They looked for holes and shafts that might

118
00:03:38,672 --> 00:03:40,544
lead down into the cave

119
00:03:40,694 --> 00:03:42,684
Thousands of people were now working to find

120
00:03:42,684 --> 00:03:44,062
the boys

121
00:03:44,212 --> 00:03:46,242
Volunteers cooked thousands of free meals for

122
00:03:46,242 --> 00:03:47,682
the rescuers

123
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:52,100
On the tenth day,

124
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,340
two British cave divers pushed further than

125
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:55,717
anyone before

126
00:03:55,867 --> 00:03:57,057
They were laying guide ropes,

127
00:03:57,057 --> 00:03:59,642
pushing deeper into the flooded tunnels

128
00:03:59,792 --> 00:04:01,342
They surfaced in a dark chamber,

129
00:04:01,342 --> 00:04:03,942
and saw lights moving on the rocks above

130
00:04:04,157 --> 00:04:04,787
One by one,

131
00:04:04,787 --> 00:04:07,387
the boys came down to the water's edge

132
00:04:07,931 --> 00:04:09,081
All thirteen were alive,

133
00:04:09,081 --> 00:04:11,520
sitting on a muddy ledge above the water

134
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:12,660
They were thin and weak,

135
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:14,098
but smiling

136
00:04:14,248 --> 00:04:16,038
'How many of you?' one diver asked

137
00:04:16,038 --> 00:04:17,589
'Thirteen,' came the answer

138
00:04:17,589 --> 00:04:18,709
'Brilliant.'

139
00:04:18,939 --> 00:04:21,009
The divers promised that many more people were

140
00:04:21,009 --> 00:04:22,400
coming to help

141
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:24,660
The video of that moment was watched around the

142
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,780
world

143
00:04:25,952 --> 00:04:26,462
Back home,

144
00:04:26,462 --> 00:04:28,542
families cried with joy

145
00:04:31,983 --> 00:04:34,237
Finding them was only the beginning

146
00:04:34,387 --> 00:04:35,070
The next day,

147
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:36,777
Thai Navy divers brought food,

148
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:38,537
medicine and blankets

149
00:04:39,043 --> 00:04:40,993
Getting out meant diving through long flooded

150
00:04:40,993 --> 00:04:41,433
tunnels,

151
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:43,473
some so narrow that divers had to squeeze

152
00:04:43,473 --> 00:04:44,524
through

153
00:04:44,674 --> 00:04:45,784
Four Thai Navy divers,

154
00:04:45,784 --> 00:04:46,864
including a doctor,

155
00:04:46,864 --> 00:04:48,664
stayed with the boys in the dark until the

156
00:04:48,664 --> 00:04:49,912
very end

157
00:04:50,062 --> 00:04:51,732
The boys had never been cave diving

158
00:04:51,732 --> 00:04:53,941
Some of them could not even swim

159
00:04:54,091 --> 00:04:55,961
The boys wrote letters to their families,

160
00:04:55,961 --> 00:04:57,796
telling them not to worry

161
00:04:57,946 --> 00:04:59,016
More rain was coming,

162
00:04:59,016 --> 00:05:01,396
which could flood the cave for months

163
00:05:01,546 --> 00:05:03,776
Some experts suggested waiting months for the

164
00:05:03,776 --> 00:05:05,402
water to go down

165
00:05:05,552 --> 00:05:07,702
And the oxygen in their chamber was starting to

166
00:05:07,702 --> 00:05:09,012
run low

167
00:05:09,162 --> 00:05:09,712
In the chamber,

168
00:05:09,712 --> 00:05:12,112
oxygen had fallen to about fifteen percent

169
00:05:12,112 --> 00:05:14,192
Normal air has twenty-one

170
00:05:17,717 --> 00:05:20,067
Divers worked day and night to place air tanks

171
00:05:20,067 --> 00:05:21,468
along the route

172
00:05:21,618 --> 00:05:23,088
Hundreds of air tanks were needed,

173
00:05:23,088 --> 00:05:25,033
carried in one by one

174
00:05:25,183 --> 00:05:26,133
On July 6th,

175
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:29,333
a former Thai Navy diver named Saman Kunan was

176
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:31,933
delivering tanks deep inside the cave

177
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:33,536
He was thirty-eight years old,

178
00:05:33,536 --> 00:05:36,064
and had left the Navy years before

179
00:05:36,214 --> 00:05:36,924
On the way back,

180
00:05:36,924 --> 00:05:38,044
he ran out of air,

181
00:05:38,044 --> 00:05:39,814
and lost his life

182
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:41,554
His dive partner tried to save him,

183
00:05:41,554 --> 00:05:43,321
but it was too late

184
00:05:43,471 --> 00:05:44,741
He had volunteered to help,

185
00:05:44,741 --> 00:05:46,932
and became a national hero

186
00:05:47,082 --> 00:05:48,072
Across Thailand,

187
00:05:48,072 --> 00:05:48,792
people mourned,

188
00:05:48,792 --> 00:05:51,392
and his story was told around the world

189
00:05:51,588 --> 00:05:53,738
His loss showed just how dangerous the rescue

190
00:05:53,738 --> 00:05:54,932
would be

191
00:05:55,082 --> 00:05:57,152
If an expert diver could lose his life,

192
00:05:57,152 --> 00:05:59,752
how could thirteen boys get out?

193
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:05,817
The rescue plan sounded almost impossible

194
00:06:06,143 --> 00:06:08,293
Dozens of the world's best cave divers had come

195
00:06:08,293 --> 00:06:09,407
together

196
00:06:09,557 --> 00:06:11,507
Each boy would wear a full-face mask,

197
00:06:11,507 --> 00:06:14,107
and be carried out by expert divers

198
00:06:14,411 --> 00:06:16,681
The divers practiced first in a swimming pool,

199
00:06:16,681 --> 00:06:19,281
with local children of the same size

200
00:06:19,531 --> 00:06:20,761
To keep them calm underwater,

201
00:06:20,761 --> 00:06:23,481
an Australian doctor who was also a cave diver

202
00:06:23,481 --> 00:06:26,081
gave each boy medicine to make him sleep

203
00:06:26,254 --> 00:06:26,964
It was risky,

204
00:06:26,964 --> 00:06:29,564
but the doctors believed it was the only way

205
00:06:29,854 --> 00:06:31,323
Then the divers would guide them,

206
00:06:31,323 --> 00:06:32,123
one by one,

207
00:06:32,123 --> 00:06:33,243
through hours of dark,

208
00:06:33,243 --> 00:06:34,683
flooded passages

209
00:06:35,183 --> 00:06:36,133
In some dry parts,

210
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:38,173
rescuers carried the boys on stretchers,

211
00:06:38,173 --> 00:06:40,734
and pulled them over rocks with ropes

212
00:06:40,884 --> 00:06:43,056
Nobody knew if it would work

213
00:06:43,206 --> 00:06:45,236
Every boy's life depended on the diver holding

214
00:06:45,236 --> 00:06:46,356
him

215
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:50,407
On July 8th,

216
00:06:50,407 --> 00:06:52,161
the rescue began

217
00:06:52,311 --> 00:06:54,141
Journalists were moved away from the cave,

218
00:06:54,141 --> 00:06:56,063
and the area was cleared

219
00:06:56,213 --> 00:06:58,683
Thirteen foreign divers and five Thai Navy

220
00:06:58,683 --> 00:07:00,185
divers went in

221
00:07:00,335 --> 00:07:01,925
Each boy was paired with a diver,

222
00:07:01,925 --> 00:07:04,125
who held him close and guided him along the

223
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:05,070
rope

224
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:07,706
The journey out took hours for each boy

225
00:07:07,856 --> 00:07:09,766
Rescuers were waiting at points along the route

226
00:07:09,766 --> 00:07:11,271
to help carry them

227
00:07:11,421 --> 00:07:12,010
That evening,

228
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:14,610
the first four boys came out alive

229
00:07:14,788 --> 00:07:15,698
Waiting outside,

230
00:07:15,698 --> 00:07:18,018
families did not yet know which boys had come

231
00:07:18,018 --> 00:07:18,946
out

232
00:07:19,096 --> 00:07:21,126
They were rushed to hospital by helicopter and

233
00:07:21,126 --> 00:07:22,246
ambulance

234
00:07:22,741 --> 00:07:25,341
Doctors said the boys were in good condition

235
00:07:29,117 --> 00:07:29,947
On July 9th,

236
00:07:29,947 --> 00:07:32,230
four more boys were carried out

237
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:33,890
It went faster than the first day,

238
00:07:33,890 --> 00:07:35,981
as the team got better at it

239
00:07:36,131 --> 00:07:36,960
On July 10th,

240
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,560
the last four boys and their coach followed

241
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,030
The four Navy divers who had stayed with the

242
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:44,236
boys were the very last to leave

243
00:07:44,386 --> 00:07:46,256
Soon after the last divers came out,

244
00:07:46,256 --> 00:07:47,416
a main pump failed,

245
00:07:47,416 --> 00:07:49,879
and the water began to rise again

246
00:07:50,029 --> 00:07:51,979
Some rescuers were still deep inside,

247
00:07:51,979 --> 00:07:53,804
and had to hurry out

248
00:07:53,954 --> 00:07:55,104
After eighteen days,

249
00:07:55,104 --> 00:07:57,125
all thirteen were safe

250
00:07:57,275 --> 00:07:58,825
The Thai Navy wrote online:

251
00:07:58,825 --> 00:08:00,825
We are not sure if this is a miracle,

252
00:08:00,825 --> 00:08:01,545
a science,

253
00:08:01,545 --> 00:08:02,814
or what

254
00:08:02,964 --> 00:08:05,364
People around the world celebrated

255
00:08:05,599 --> 00:08:07,789
Football teams and players around the world

256
00:08:07,789 --> 00:08:08,669
sent messages,

257
00:08:08,669 --> 00:08:11,269
and invited the boys to big matches

258
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:16,760
The boys spent about a week in hospital,

259
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,395
and recovered well

260
00:08:18,545 --> 00:08:18,975
At first,

261
00:08:18,975 --> 00:08:21,015
families could only see them through a glass

262
00:08:21,015 --> 00:08:21,455
window,

263
00:08:21,455 --> 00:08:23,249
in case of infection

264
00:08:23,399 --> 00:08:24,109
On average,

265
00:08:24,109 --> 00:08:26,709
each boy had lost about two kilograms

266
00:08:27,416 --> 00:08:27,766
Later,

267
00:08:27,766 --> 00:08:29,926
most of them spent time as novice monks,

268
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,526
to honor the diver who gave his life

269
00:08:32,676 --> 00:08:34,466
They lived at a temple for several days,

270
00:08:34,466 --> 00:08:36,226
praying and meditating

271
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,109
Four of them,

272
00:08:37,109 --> 00:08:38,470
who had no nationality,

273
00:08:38,470 --> 00:08:40,870
were later granted Thai citizenship

274
00:08:41,094 --> 00:08:41,524
Later,

275
00:08:41,524 --> 00:08:41,964
books,

276
00:08:41,964 --> 00:08:44,564
documentaries and films told their story

277
00:08:45,112 --> 00:08:47,668
The divers were celebrated as heroes

278
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,768
But many of them said the real heroes were

279
00:08:49,768 --> 00:08:50,328
the boys,

280
00:08:50,328 --> 00:08:52,601
who stayed calm in the dark

281
00:08:52,751 --> 00:08:53,061
Today,

282
00:08:53,061 --> 00:08:54,341
the boys are grown up,

283
00:08:54,341 --> 00:08:56,941
and some of them still play football

284
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,120
Around ten thousand people took part in the

285
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,240
rescue

286
00:09:03,432 --> 00:09:05,062
That included about ninety divers,

287
00:09:05,062 --> 00:09:07,415
from Thailand and around the world

288
00:09:07,565 --> 00:09:08,595
Divers and doctors,

289
00:09:08,595 --> 00:09:10,435
but also cooks who fed the rescuers,

290
00:09:10,435 --> 00:09:12,535
and farmers who let their fields flood with

291
00:09:12,535 --> 00:09:13,755
pumped water

292
00:09:13,935 --> 00:09:15,295
Many of them were volunteers,

293
00:09:15,295 --> 00:09:17,413
who simply showed up to help

294
00:09:17,563 --> 00:09:19,273
It showed what people can do when the whole

295
00:09:19,273 --> 00:09:20,977
world works together

296
00:09:21,127 --> 00:09:21,477
Today,

297
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:23,317
visitors come to the cave to learn about the

298
00:09:23,317 --> 00:09:24,437
rescue

299
00:09:24,623 --> 00:09:25,013
Today,

300
00:09:25,013 --> 00:09:28,013
a statue of Saman Kunan stands near the cave,

301
00:09:28,013 --> 00:09:30,613
to remember the hero who did not come back

302
00:09:31,055 --> 00:09:32,245
During the rainy season,

303
00:09:32,245 --> 00:09:33,325
the cave is closed,

304
00:09:33,325 --> 00:09:35,573
just as the old sign warned

305
00:09:35,723 --> 00:09:37,433
It is a reminder to respect nature,

306
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:39,393
and to never give up hope

307
00:09:39,543 --> 00:09:41,943
And thirteen lives were saved

308
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:43,440
Twelve boys

309
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,120
One coach

310
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,135
Eighteen days in the dark

311
00:09:46,285 --> 00:09:47,435
Thousands of helpers,

312
00:09:47,435 --> 00:09:49,948
and one hero who never came home

313
00:09:50,098 --> 00:09:50,968
What would you have done,

314
00:09:50,968 --> 00:09:52,515
trapped in that cave?

315
00:09:52,665 --> 00:09:54,083
Tell me in the comments

316
00:09:54,233 --> 00:09:56,833
Subscribe so you don't miss the next episode
